On Sun, 19 May 2024 at 16:45, Yash Shinde <Yash.Shinde@windriver.com> wrote:

> I applied your patchset for AB failures locally and checked the rust
> testsuite, but I didn't see any failures there. I applied all the 4
> patches from the following patch series:
> https://lists.openembedded.org/g/openembedded-core/message/199464
>
> Is there any other patchset apart from this, that also needs to be
> applied or am I missing something?

I don't think so; you only need to apply the four (now five in v2)
patches on top of master, initialize the build with poky defaults (.
oe-init-buld-env), and run the selftest.

> I also saw the failure logs sent by Alexandre Belloni but cannot
> reproduce those as well.
> (https://lists.openembedded.org/g/openembedded-core/message/199540).
>

That one is caused by running the test with host python; this isn't correct and
native python should be used, just as in rust recipe. I have a patch
for this, selftest
still passes, so I'm going to send a v2 of the patchset. Unfortunately
I can't test this
on the autobuilder now, as it is overloaded with a-full builds.

> Can you share the log file or the failures here? (Log file is present at
> "build-st/tmp/work/cortexa57-poky-linux/rust/1.75.0/results-log.txt")

That file isn't being created because the failure happens earlier in
runCmd(), causes an exception and prevents the lines that write it out
from being executed. I re-ran the selftest with shell redirect, and
attached the output.

Alex

